findings.body:
The new helper returns true only when `user != null`. Before this change, the conditional-UI webauthn data was filled precisely when the user was NOT yet identified (`context.getUser() == null`).

The helper is now used in `authenticate()` (line 115) and in `challenge(context, error, field)` (line 137). As a result, the initial login page, where no user is set, no longer gets `fillContextForm` called. That means:
- no challenge auth note is stored;
- no `ENABLE_WEBAUTHN_CONDITIONAL_UI` attribute is set;
- the error re-render after a bad username or password also loses passkeys.

Normal passkey login stops working, and tests like `webauthnLoginWithDiscoverableKey` / `passwordLoginWithNonDiscoverableKey`, which expect `form#webauth` on first load, would fail. The check should not exclude the `user == null` case; most likely it should drop the user condition entirely.
